    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's hard to explain, but the way they describe it feels so much like a prank. like there's this tiny, chaotic presence that just loves to mess things up at the most inconvenient moments. i know you're saying it's just error signals, but is there really no way to view these \"little troublemakers\" in the nervous system as something more than just math errors? like, can the brain's attempts at recalibration actually feel like something external is purposefully causing mischief or being a little pest in the middle of a set?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
